<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Operating
lease assets are included within operating lease right-of-use assets, and the corresponding operating lease obligation on the consolidated
balance sheets as of June 30, 2026 and March 31, 2026 in accordance with ASC 842, <i>Leases</i>. The Company has elected not to present
short-term leases as these leases have a lease term of 12 months or less at lease inception and do not contain purchase options or renewal
terms that the Company is reasonably certain to exercise. All other lease assets and lease liabilities are recognized based on the present
value of lease payments over the lease term at commencement date. Because most of the Company&#8217;s leases do not provide an implicit
rate of return, the Company used an incremental borrowing rate based on the information available at adoption date in determining the
present value of lease payments.</span></p>

